  "answer": "Citation complaints fell sharply after the April 2026 release. Q1 citation-accuracy tickets were 72 in January, 79 in February, and 88 in March, while Q2 tickets dropped to 42 in April, 31 in May, and 24 in June [NL-011#NL-011-S05]. The Q2 report confirms complaints \"decreased significantly\" [NL-016#NL-016-S04] and \"dropped significantly\" [NL-011#NL-011-S03]. However, they did not reach zero—the remaining May and June tickets are almost entirely tied to scanned, image-only PDFs, where TutorChat struggles to establish citation anchors and often links to the file start [NL-011#NL-011-S05].\n\nThe planned product work that directly addresses the remaining scanned-document problem is the **Advanced OCR Pipeline**. Per the Q1 action items, Product must finalize requirements for an integrated OCR pipeline to address scanned PDF challenges, with a target to launch the OCR pilot by August 2026 [NL-010#NL-010-S10]. Per the later discussion, this pipeline is scheduled for release in August 2026 and will automatically extract text and layout structures from scanned files, enabling page-specific citations [NL-024#NL-024-S04].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
